    {
      "id": "p0235-b008",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In today's computer age, writers regularly rely on automatic spell-checking and search-and-replace tools to fix problematic text. Translators rely on these tools all the time, too. Of course, these tools can actually introduce new problems into a translation if used improperly. This phenomenon is rare, but when it occurs, it can harm the quality of the full, final product.",
        "raw": "In today's computer age, writers regularly rely on automatic spell-checking\nand search-and-replace tools to fix problematic text. Translators rely on\nthese tools all the time, too. Of course, these tools can actually introduce\nnew problems into a translation if used improperly. This phenomenon is\nrare, but when it occurs, it can harm the quality of the full, final product.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.12535687,
          0.78008571,
          0.6768706,
          0.85927143
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.12404571,
          0.77937143,
          0.67818176,
          0.86034286
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          43,
          44,
          45,
          46,
          47
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "在电脑时代，作者经常用自动拼写检查、查找替换来修正文稿，译者也一样。不过，使用不当时，这些工具也会给译文引入新问题。这种情况不常见，但一旦发生，就会损害最终成品的整体质量。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
